AltoConvexCreditLineMarket::initializeV2(uint256)
├── given a proxy initialized only through initialize
│   └── it should have zero treasury share and use basis-point precision
├── when called on the implementation directly
│   └── it should revert with InvalidInitialization
├── when caller is not owner
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount and preserve the current share
│   └── it should leave the reinitializer available to the owner
├── when the treasury share exceeds the full allocation
│   ├── it should revert with AltoCreditMarketInvalidInput and preserve the current share
│   └── it should permit retrying with a valid share
├── when the owner initializes a valid share
│   ├── it should set treasuryInterestBps and emit SetTreasuryInterestBps and Initialized version 2
│   ├── it should accept zero and full treasury allocations
│   └── it should reject a second initialization even when the first share was zero
└── when fees accrued before initialization
    ├── it should preserve market accounting and balances without accruing interest or claiming fees
    └── it should apply the configured split when those fees are subsequently claimed
